{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Since Asciidoctor’s primary focus is on converting documents efficiently, it does not attempt to store information about all assets it comes across while processing the document. However, such information can be useful for analyzing the document or for use in extensions. Therefore, Asciidoctor provides a flag to catalog certain additional assets. This page explains how to enable this catalog and how to access it."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The asset catalog provides a table of select assets grouped by type that are discovered while processing the document. This table is stored on the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "catalog"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " property of the document model."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "When this feature is enabled, the processor catalogs the following assets:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "ulist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "links (but not xrefs) (key: "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": ":links"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ")"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "block or inline images (key: "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": ":images"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ")"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "style": null,
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The processor always cataloged the following assets, regardless of this setting:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "ulist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "block or inline anchors (key: "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": ":refs"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ")"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "footnotes (key: "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": ":footnotes"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ")"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "style": null,
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Generally speaking, inline elements are not cataloged until conversion. Therefore, they’re only available after the document has been converted, not after it has been loaded. However, inline anchors are an exception."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Inline anchors in paragraphs and list items are cataloged when the document is parsed. However, the scan for inline anchors happens before inline passthroughs are processed. Therefore, to escape an inline anchor, you must use a backslash instead of an inline passthrough."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_what_assets_are_cataloged",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "What assets are cataloged?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Whether the processor catalogs assets (specifically links and images) is controlled from the API using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ":catalog_assets"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " option. The value of this option is a boolean. If the value is "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "false"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (default), assets are not cataloged. If the value is "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "true"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", assets are cataloged. The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ":catalog_assets"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " option is accepted by all "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "entrypoint methods"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "index.html#entrypoints"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (e.g., Asciidoctor#load_file)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Here’s an example of how to catalog assets when using the API:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "doc = Asciidoctor.convert_file 'doc.adoc', safe: :safe, catalog_assets: true"
              }
            ],
            "language": "ruby",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Notice that we’ve used the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "convert_file"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method instead of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "load_file"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method. This ensures that inline assets are included in the catalog as well."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you need to enable the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ":catalog_assets"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " option when using the CLI, you’ll need to require the following extension:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Asciidoctor::Extensions.register do\n  preprocessor do\n    process do |doc, reader|\n      doc.instance_variable_set :@options, ((doc.instance_variable_get :@options).merge catalog_assets: true)\n      nil\n    end\n  end\nend"
              }
            ],
            "language": "ruby",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "enable-catalog-assets-preprocessor.rb"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Now that you’ve configured the processor to catalog assets, you can access them from the document object. Let’s explore it."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_set_catalog_assets_option",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Set :catalog_assets option"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Assets which have been cataloged are available from the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "catalog"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " property on the document model (i.e., the parsed document). The catalog is a Ruby hash. The keys are the asset families (e.g., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ":links"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ":images"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", etc). The value of each key is an array of assets. The asset object varies by family."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Let’s look at an example of how to access links, images, and refs from the asset catalog."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Start by creating the following AsciiDoc file named "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "doc.adoc"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "emphasis",
                    "roles": [
                      "path"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "listing",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "You can learn about Asciidoctor at https://docs.asciidoctor.org.\nThe Asciidoctor source repo is hosted on https://github.com[GitHub].\n\nimage::screenshot.png[]\n\nIf you see image:green-check.png[], it means the job was successful."
                  }
                ],
                "language": "asciidoc",
                "roles": [],
                "title": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "doc.adoc"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Now, convert this file using Asciidoctor with the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": ":catalog_assets"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " option enabled:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "listing",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "doc = Asciidoctor.convert_file 'doc.adoc', safe: :safe, catalog_assets: true"
                  }
                ],
                "language": "ruby",
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Let’s see what links the processor found:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "listing",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "links = doc.catalog[:links]\nputs \"Found #{links.size} links:\"\nputs links"
                  }
                ],
                "language": "ruby",
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "You’ll see the following output:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "literal",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Found 2 links:\nhttps://docs.asciidoctor.org\nhttps://github.com"
                  }
                ],
                "language": null,
                "roles": [
                  "output"
                ],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The value of the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": ":links"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " key is an array of unique URLs found in the document. The entry does not include the link text, only the URL itself."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "section",
            "id": "_links",
            "level": 2,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ":links"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Let’s add some images to the document."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "listing",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "//...\n\nimage::screenshot.png[]\n\nIf you see image:green-check.png[], it means the job was successful."
                  }
                ],
                "language": "asciidoc",
                "roles": [],
                "title": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "doc.adoc"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Now, convert this file using Asciidoctor with the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": ":catalog_assets"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " option enabled:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "listing",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "doc = Asciidoctor.convert_file 'doc.adoc', safe: :safe, catalog_assets: true"
                  }
                ],
                "language": "ruby",
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Let’s see what images the processor found:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "listing",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "images = doc.catalog[:images]\nputs \"Found #{images.size} images:\"\nputs images"
                  }
                ],
                "language": "ruby",
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "You’ll see the following output:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "literal",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Found 2 images:\nscreenshot.png\ngreen-check.png"
                  }
                ],
                "language": null,
                "roles": [
                  "output"
                ],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The value of the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": ":images"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " key is an array of images (by occurrence) found in the document. While it looks like the value of each entry is a relative path string, there’s actually more information there."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Each entry in the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": ":images"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " collection is an ImageReference object. This object appears as a relative path string when printed (which explains the observed behavior). An ImageReference contains the following properties:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "The image path relative to the value of imagesdir."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "target"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "The value of the imagesdir attribute at the time the image was processed."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "imagesdir"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Let’s assume the images are located in the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "images"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "emphasis",
                    "roles": [
                      "path"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " folder, and we have set the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "imagesdir"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " attribute on the document accordingly."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "listing",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "= Document Title\n:imagesdir: images\n\n//...\n\nimage::screenshot.png[]\n\nIf you see image:green-check.png[], it means the job was successful."
                  }
                ],
                "language": "asciidoc",
                "roles": [],
                "title": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "doc.adoc"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "You can print the full location to the images as follows:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "listing",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "images = doc.catalog[:images]\nputs \"Found #{images.size} images:\"\ndocdir = doc.attr 'docdir'\nputs images.map {|image| File.join docdir, image.imagesdir.to_s, image.target }"
                  }
                ],
                "language": "ruby",
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "In the output, the image references will be shown as absolute paths."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "section",
            "id": "_images",
            "level": 2,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ":images"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "In addition to images and links, you can also access all targetable references (i.e., elements that have an ID). First, let’s add some referenceable elements to our document."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "listing",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
